discussion_comments.comment_body:
You can put the previous commitData in state as well. Writing to a ref during render is unsafe: https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect#adjusting-some-state-when-a-prop-changes
```suggestion
  const [prevCommitData, setPrevCommitData] = useState<Array<CommitDataFrontend>>(commitData);
  if (prevCommitData !== commitData) {
    setPrevCommitData(prevCommitData)
    selectCommitIndex(commitData.length > 0 ? 0 : null);
  }
```

